Common Media Interference
  1.EMI/RFI - Electromagnetic Interference (EMI) and Radio Frequency Interference (RFI) can interfere with electrical signals.
    Examples:
      Electric motors
      Fluorescent lighting
      Radio signals
  2.Crosstalk - Crosstalk occurs when the signal from one wire interferes with a nearby wire.
  3.Attenuation - Attenuation is the weakening of a signal as it travels over distance.
  Simple relationship:
    Longer distance → More signal loss
